# OmniOS — local configuration
#
# V1 runs completely without any of these. Every value below unlocks a real
# integration that replaces a deterministic local simulation. Nothing here is
# required to start the OS.

# --- Where the workspace lives on disk -------------------------------------
# Defaults to `.omnios-data/` inside the repo (git-ignored).
# Point this at an iCloud/Dropbox folder to sync across machines.
OMNIOS_DATA_DIR=

# How the workspace is stored inside that directory. Leave empty for plain
# JSON files, one per scope. Set to `sqlite` for a single SQLite database
# (omnios.sqlite) — an existing JSON workspace is imported on first run and
# the JSON files are left untouched, so switching back is always safe.
OMNIOS_STORE=

# --- Language model providers ----------------------------------------------
# With no key set, OmniOS uses the deterministic local reasoning simulator:
# the Executive Assistant still routes, delegates, plans and explains itself,
# but the wording is generated locally and is clearly labelled as simulated.
#
# Provider keys can live here for local dev, but the vault is the real home:
# Connections -> Keys and secrets, under these same names. The vault is read
# first and never lands on the workspace root.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OLLAMA_API_KEY=

# Which provider the Executive Assistant uses. Auto-detects from whichever key
# is present when unset; set it to force one of: anthropic | openai | ollama.
OMNIOS_ASSISTANT_PROVIDER=

# Model used by the Executive Assistant when a key is present, and per-provider
# overrides for the OpenAI-compatible and Ollama paths.
OMNIOS_ASSISTANT_MODEL=claude-opus-4-5
OMNIOS_OPENAI_MODEL=
OMNIOS_OLLAMA_MODEL=

# --- Feature seams (all inert in V1) ---------------------------------------
# Banking / accounting / payment providers for the Finance Center.
OMNIOS_FINANCE_PROVIDER=
# Image / video model provider for the Creative Studio.
OMNIOS_CREATIVE_PROVIDER=
# Source feed for the AI Intelligence Center.
OMNIOS_INTEL_FEED_URL=

# --- Approvals on your phone (Telegram) ------------------------------------
# The bot token is a credential and belongs in the vault, under exactly this
# name: Connections -> Keys and secrets -> TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN. It is read only
# when a message is sent and never lands on the workspace root.
#
# This secret is different: Telegram echoes it back as a header on every webhook
# delivery, so it is how the endpoint knows a POST is really from Telegram.
# Without it the webhook accepts nothing at all — it fails closed, so buttons
# would arrive and do nothing rather than anyone being able to press them.
#   openssl rand -hex 32
TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Then point Telegram at the route (needs a public URL — a tunnel is fine):
#   curl -F "url=https://<host>/api/telegram/webhook" \
#        -F "secret_token=$TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET" \
#        https://api.telegram.org/bot<token>/setWebhook
